# TypeScript Strictness

<version>1.0.0</version>

## Context
- All TypeScript and TSX files
- Applies to all new and modified code

## Requirements
- Use explicit types for all function parameters and return values
- No usage of `any` type unless absolutely necessary and justified with a comment
- All components and helpers must be typed
- Resolve all TypeScript errors before commit

## Examples
<example>
function add(a: number, b: number): number { return a + b }
</example>
<example type="invalid">
function add(a, b) { return a + b }
</example>
